[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Hierarchical Architecture and Its Failure Mode (Part 3 of 3)","textKn":"ಶ್ರೇಣಿ ವಾಸ್ತುಶಿಲ್ಪ ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ವೈಫಲ್ಯ ವಿಧಾನ (ಭಾಗ 3 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 3 of 3: choosing sequential, flat or hierarchical from the structure of a task, capability checks, a gate before delegation with three scenarios, an evidence-reference gate, a reconciliation policy and a generated fitness document. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind a three-level hierarchy of agents and how it fails (a wrong delegation that every worker executes faithfully, narrowed requirements, unknown turned into certainty, reconciliation loops, provenance, a pattern chooser, a gate before delegation and a generated fitness document), not the real software, and managers and workers are scripted functions with canned findings, the scoring rules are our own heuristic, the evidence references are mock strings and no real engineering, legal or finance review happens, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied, so the labs are our own implementation. The CrewAI and LangGraph material in the lesson is conceptual and was not run, and the depth-2 remark is a design heuristic and not a proven threshold. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 3ನೆಯದು: ಕೆಲಸದ ರಚನೆಯಿಂದ sequential, flat ಅಥವಾ hierarchical ಆರಿಸುವುದು, ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ, ಮೂರು ಸನ್ನಿವೇಶಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ನಿಯೋಜನೆಯ ಮೊದಲಿನ ದ್ವಾರ, ಸಾಕ್ಷಿ-ಉಲ್ಲೇಖ ದ್ವಾರ, ಸಮನ್ವಯ ನೀತಿ ಮತ್ತು ರಚಿತ fitness ದಾಖಲೆ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು ಏಜೆಂಟ್‌ಗಳ ಮೂರು-ಹಂತದ ಶ್ರೇಣಿ ಮತ್ತು ಅದು ಹೇಗೆ ವಿಫಲವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ (ಪ್ರತಿ ಕೆಲಸಗಾರ ನಿಷ್ಠೆಯಿಂದ ನಡೆಸುವ ತಪ್ಪು ನಿಯೋಜನೆ, ಕಿರಿದಾದ ಅವಶ್ಯಕತೆಗಳು, ನಿಶ್ಚಿತತೆಯಾಗಿ ಬದಲಾದ ಅಜ್ಞಾತ, ಸಮನ್ವಯ ಲೂಪ್‌ಗಳು, provenance, ಮಾದರಿ ಆಯ್ಕೆಕಾರ, ನಿಯೋಜನೆಯ ಮೊದಲಿನ ದ್ವಾರ ಮತ್ತು ರಚಿತ fitness ದಾಖಲೆ) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಮ್ಯಾನೇಜರ್‌ಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಕೆಲಸಗಾರರು ಸಿದ್ಧ ಕಂಡುಹಿಡಿಕೆಗಳ ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್ ಕಾರ್ಯಗಳು, ಅಂಕ ನಿಯಮಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಹ್ಯೂರಿಸ್ಟಿಕ್, ಸಾಕ್ಷಿ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಗಳು ನಕಲಿ ಸ್ಟ್ರಿಂಗ್‌ಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವುದೇ ನಿಜವಾದ engineering, legal ಅಥವಾ finance ವಿಮರ್ಶೆ ನಡೆಯುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ನೀಡಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ. lesson ನ CrewAI ಮತ್ತು LangGraph ವಿಷಯ ಪರಿಕಲ್ಪನಾತ್ಮಕ ಮತ್ತು ಓಡಿಸಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು depth-2 ಟಿಪ್ಪಣಿ ವಿನ್ಯಾಸ ಹ್ಯೂರಿಸ್ಟಿಕ್, ಸಾಬೀತಾದ ಮಿತಿಯಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Use a Hierarchy Only When the Problem Has One","textKn":"ಸಮಸ್ಯೆಗೆ ಇದ್ದರೆ ಮಾತ್ರ ಶ್ರೇಣಿ ಬಳಸಿ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Choosing a Pattern and Running It Safely","headingKn":"ಮಾದರಿ ಆರಿಸುವುದು ಮತ್ತು ಸುರಕ್ಷಿತವಾಗಿ ಓಡಿಸುವುದು","bodyEn":"The last question of the lesson is whether a task needs a hierarchy at all. This part writes a transparent chooser that looks at dependencies, independent branches, sub-teams, reconciliation budget and tracing, and runs it on four tasks. It then runs the hierarchy with the gates in place: a capability check, a plan check before any department runs, an evidence-reference rule, a reconciliation policy that classifies a disagreement and escalates when it must, a count of the calls such a hierarchy makes, and a generated skeleton of the fitness document the lesson asks for.","bodyKn":"lesson ನ ಕೊನೆಯ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆ ಕೆಲಸಕ್ಕೆ ಶ್ರೇಣಿ ಬೇಕೇ ಎಂಬುದು. ಈ ಭಾಗವು ಅವಲಂಬನೆಗಳು, ಸ್ವತಂತ್ರ ಶಾಖೆಗಳು, ಉಪ-ತಂಡಗಳು, ಸಮನ್ವಯ ಬಜೆಟ್ ಮತ್ತು ಟ್ರೇಸಿಂಗ್ ನೋಡುವ ಪಾರದರ್ಶಕ ಆಯ್ಕೆಕಾರನನ್ನು ಬರೆದು ನಾಲ್ಕು ಕೆಲಸಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ನಂತರ ದ್ವಾರಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಶ್ರೇಣಿ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ: ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ, ಯಾವುದೇ ವಿಭಾಗ ಓಡುವ ಮೊದಲು ಯೋಜನೆ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ, ಸಾಕ್ಷಿ-ಉಲ್ಲೇಖ ನಿಯಮ, ಭಿನ್ನಾಭಿಪ್ರಾಯ ವರ್ಗೀಕರಿಸಿ ಅಗತ್ಯವಿದ್ದಾಗ ಎಸ್ಕಲೇಟ್ ಮಾಡುವ ಸಮನ್ವಯ ನೀತಿ, ಅಂತಹ ಶ್ರೇಣಿ ಮಾಡುವ ಕರೆಗಳ ಎಣಿಕೆ, ಮತ್ತು lesson ಕೇಳುವ fitness ದಾಖಲೆಯ ರಚಿತ ಅಸ್ಥಿಪಂಜರ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Pattern Fitness","headingKn":"ಮಾದರಿ ಹೊಂದಾಣಿಕೆ","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">pick the simplest pattern that keeps the original request safe</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">choose</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">by dependencies</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">gate</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">before any worker runs</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">evidence</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">cited or not accepted</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">escalate</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">when no progress</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">pick the simplest pattern that keeps the original request safe</text></svg>","captionEn":"Choose by dependency and sub-team structure, then add the gates.","captionKn":"ಅವಲಂಬನೆ ಮತ್ತು ಉಪ-ತಂಡ ರಚನೆಯಿಂದ ಆರಿಸಿ, ನಂತರ ದ್ವಾರಗಳನ್ನು ಸೇರಿಸಿ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The six experiments","headingKn":"ಆರು ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","headers":["Experiment","What it checks"],"rows":[["pattern choice","four tasks mapped to sequential, flat or hierarchical"],["capabilities","who may be assigned which domain"],["scenarios","accepted, rejected before running, needs review"],["evidence gate","a report that cites nothing"],["reconciliation","budget and no-progress escalation"],["cost and document","12 calls, 28000 tokens and a generated skeleton"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"hi_3.py","headingEn":"The chooser","headingKn":"ಆಯ್ಕೆಕಾರ","descEn":"TaskProfile describes dependency strength, branches, sub-teams, budget and tracing, and recommend_pattern maps it to a pattern with a reason.","descKn":"TaskProfile ಅವಲಂಬನೆ ಬಲ, ಶಾಖೆಗಳು, ಉಪ-ತಂಡಗಳು, ಬಜೆಟ್ ಮತ್ತು ಟ್ರೇಸಿಂಗ್ ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು recommend_pattern ಅದನ್ನು ಕಾರಣದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮಾದರಿಗೆ ಮ್ಯಾಪ್ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"class Pattern(str, Enum):
    SEQUENTIAL = "sequential"
    FLAT = "flat_supervisor"
    HIERARCHICAL = "hierarchical"


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class TaskProfile:
    description: str
    independent_branches: int
    branches_with_subteams: int
    dependency_strength: int
    reconciliation_budget: int
    observability_ready: bool


def recommend_pattern(t):
    if t.independent_branches < 1:
        raise ValueError("At least one branch is required")
    if t.dependency_strength >= 3 or t.independent_branches == 1:
        return Pattern.SEQUENTIAL, "strong dependencies or one branch"
    if t.branches_with_subteams >= 2 and t.reconciliation_budget >= 1 and t.observability_ready:
        return Pattern.HIERARCHICAL, "independent branches with sub-teams and the controls to manage them"
    return Pattern.FLAT, "independent work without enough sub-team structure or controls""}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"hi_3.py","headingEn":"Gates and policy","headingKn":"ದ್ವಾರಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ನೀತಿ","descEn":"validate_plan checks coverage and capability before delegation, run_workflow accepts only supported findings with evidence references, and reconcile_policy escalates on an exhausted budget or no new evidence.","descKn":"validate_plan ನಿಯೋಜನೆಗೆ ಮೊದಲು ವ್ಯಾಪ್ತಿ ಮತ್ತು ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, run_workflow ಸಾಕ್ಷಿ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಗಳಿರುವ supported ಕಂಡುಹಿಡಿಕೆಗಳನ್ನು ಮಾತ್ರ ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು reconcile_policy ಬಜೆಟ್ ಮುಗಿದಾಗ ಅಥವಾ ಹೊಸ ಸಾಕ್ಷಿ ಇಲ್ಲದಾಗ ಎಸ್ಕಲೇಟ್ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"CAPABILITIES = {"engineering_manager": {"engineering"}, "legal_manager": {"legal"}, "finance_manager": {"finance"}}
MANAGER_OF = {"engineering": "engineering_manager", "legal": "legal_manager", "finance": "finance_manager"}


def validate_assignment(manager, domain):
    return domain in CAPABILITIES.get(manager, set())


def validate_plan(required, plan):
    errors = []
    missing = sorted(set(required) - set(plan))
    if missing:
        errors.append(f"Missing required domains: {missing}")
    for d in plan:
        if not validate_assignment(MANAGER_OF.get(d, ""), d):
            errors.append(f"No capable manager for {d}")
    return errors


def run_workflow(required, plan, legal_status="supported", drop_refs=None):
    errors = validate_plan(required, plan)
    if errors:
        return {"status": "rejected", "errors": errors, "reports": 0}
    findings = {"engineering": ("success", "supported"), "legal": ("success", legal_status), "finance": ("success", "supported")}
    reports = [{"domain": d, "execution": findings[d][0], "evidence": findings[d][1], "refs": [f"mock://{d}"] if findings[d][1] != "unknown" else []} for d in plan]
    for r in reports:
        if r["domain"] == drop_refs:
            r["refs"] = []
    unresolved = [r["domain"] for r in reports if r["evidence"] == "unknown"]
    if unresolved:
        return {"status": "needs_review", "errors": [f"Unresolved requirement: {d}" for d in unresolved], "reports": len(reports)}
    uncited = [r["domain"] for r in reports if not r["refs"]]
    if uncited:
        return {"status": "needs_review", "errors": [f"Missing evidence references: {d}" for d in uncited], "reports": len(reports)}
    return {"status": "accepted", "errors": [], "reports": len(reports)}


def classify(kind):
    return {"factual": "targeted evidence request", "scope": "clarify the task contract", "policy": "apply the explicit decision policy", "uncertainty": "compare the evidence"}[kind]


def reconcile_policy(attempts_used, budget, new_evidence):
    if new_evidence:
        return "continue" if attempts_used < budget else "escalate_budget_exhausted"
    return "escalate_no_progress""}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"hi_3.py","headingEn":"The experiments","headingKn":"ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() runs the six experiments in order and prints the real result of each.","descKn":"main() ಆರು ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳನ್ನು ಕ್ರಮವಾಗಿ ಓಡಿಸಿ ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದರ ನಿಜ ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಮುದ್ರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely running: picking a pattern from the structure of the task")
    tasks = [TaskProfile("research, draft, edit", 1, 0, 4, 1, True), TaskProfile("three independent reviews", 3, 0, 0, 1, True),
             TaskProfile("enterprise launch readiness", 4, 4, 1, 2, True), TaskProfile("enterprise launch, no tracing", 4, 4, 1, 2, False)]
    for t in tasks:
        p, why = recommend_pattern(t)
        print(f"{t.description}: {p.value} ({why})")
    print("a chain of dependent steps gets a sequential pipeline, three independent reviews get a flat supervisor, and four departments with sub-teams get a hierarchy only when tracing is ready, otherwise the same task falls back to a flat supervisor; the rules and thresholds are our own heuristic and have not been calibrated on real outcomes.")

    section("2. Genuinely running: capability checks")
    print("legal_manager for legal:", validate_assignment("legal_manager", "legal"), "| finance_manager for legal:", validate_assignment("finance_manager", "legal"), "| unknown manager:", validate_assignment("ghost", "legal"))
    print("a legal task is accepted for the legal manager and refused for the finance manager, and an unregistered manager has no capabilities; a capability match checks who may do a job and not whether the plan covers the request, so both checks are needed.")

    section("3. Genuinely running: three scenarios with a gate before delegation")
    required = ["engineering", "legal"]
    for label, plan, legal in (("happy path", ["engineering", "legal"], "supported"), ("legal swapped for finance", ["engineering", "finance"], "supported"), ("unknown legal evidence", ["engineering", "legal"], "unknown")):
        print(f"{label}: {run_workflow(required, plan, legal)}")
    print("the correct plan is accepted with two reports, the swapped plan is rejected before any department runs and so has zero reports, and the plan with unknown legal evidence runs both departments and ends as needs_review instead of being accepted; accepted here means the scripted structural rules held and not that a product is ready.")

    section("4. Genuinely running: a finding that cites nothing")
    print("with references:", run_workflow(required, ["engineering", "legal"]))
    print("engineering cites nothing:", run_workflow(required, ["engineering", "legal"], drop_refs="engineering"))
    print("the same plan and the same supported findings are accepted when every report cites a reference and end as needs_review when the engineering report cites none, naming the department; the references in this lab are mock strings, so the gate checks that something is cited and cannot check that the cited thing exists or supports the claim.")

    section("5. Genuinely running: what kind of disagreement it is, and when to stop")
    for kind in ("factual", "scope", "policy", "uncertainty"):
        print(f"{kind}: {classify(kind)}")
    print("attempt 1 of 2 with new evidence:", reconcile_policy(1, 2, True), "| attempt 2 of 2 with new evidence:", reconcile_policy(2, 2, True), "| attempt 1 with no new evidence:", reconcile_policy(1, 2, False))
    print("each kind of disagreement gets its own response, and the policy escalates when the budget is used up or when an attempt brings no new evidence, instead of asking the departments to agree again; engineering saying deployable and legal saying not approved can both be true, so the final report keeps both statements.")

    section("6. Genuinely computing: management calls, tokens and a generated fitness document")
    calls = 2 + 2 * 3 + 4
    tokens = 8 * 2000 + 4 * 3000
    print("calls for a top manager of 2, two sub-managers of 3 each and four workers of 1:", calls, "| tokens at 8 manager calls of 2000 and 4 worker calls of 3000:", tokens)
    required_sections = ["Purpose", "Task description", "Organizational structure", "Architecture alternatives", "Fitness assessment", "Recommendation", "Required safeguards", "Failure modes", "Acceptance criteria", "Verification plan", "Final decision"]
    text = "# Hierarchy Fitness Evaluation\n\n" + "\n\n".join(f"## {s}\n\nTo be completed for this task." for s in required_sections)
    path = os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), "skill-hierarchy-fitness.md")
    with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(text)
    written = open(path, encoding="utf-8").read()
    print("sections written:", written.count("\n## "), "| all required headings present:", all(f"## {s}" in written for s in required_sections))
    print("twelve model calls and 28000 tokens are what the example numbers add up to for this shape of hierarchy, and a generated skeleton with eleven headings is not an evaluation until someone fills it in; the file is written to a temporary folder and the call and token figures are example inputs and not measurements.")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
